Abstract = {Mental Health and Well-Being affects performance and professional
   success. Loneliness at work is a relative new topic of research.
   Loneliness is associated with suicidal ideation, is predictor for
   depression symptoms and is a risk factor for dementia and high blood
   pressure. In a recent study run in an hospital of the romanian sanitary
   system, results have shown that loneliness at work explains some of the
   variations of the performance dimensions. In this article are discussed
   findings about loneliness at work and future research or intervention
   possibilities.},
