   CA, MAY   28, 2005},
Organization = {Amer Psychol Soc},
Abstract = {Does the appearance of an instructor and the,format of the class
   influence student grades and learning? We tested this question with 861
   undergraduate students who completed an online questionnaire rating
   their instructors. Students were equally spread across class year and
   were from different majors. We used multiple regression analyses and
   found that likable, good-looking, well-dressed, and approachable
   teachers had students who said they learned more., had higher grades,
   and liked the class better.},
