   Scientific Knowledge to Inform Policy and Practice in Disaster Risk
   Reduction, Bangkok, THAILAND, NOV 27-29, 2017},
Organization = {Univ Huddersfield, Global Disaster Resilience Ctr; Naresuan Univ; Chiang
   Mai Univ; Asian Disaster Preparedness Ctr},
Abstract = {The potential of risk communication as tool for reducing the devastating
   impacts posited by disaster hazards on human lives and property has been
   discussed extensively in literature. Most risk communication studies and
   strategies focus on awareness creation and education on disaster
   hazards. However, awareness creation and education on disaster hazards
   do not necessary translate into preparatory attitude and behaviour
   towards disaster hazards. Frantic efforts are required to persuade and
   motivate people at risk to convert hazard awareness and education into
   preparation towards disaster hazards. Against this backdrop, this paper
   develops a conceptual model through literature review to facilitate and
   enhance disaster preparedness through risk communication. (C) 2018 The
   Authors. Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
